h now as your path to durable capability (especially given you've already lost 2 engineers — concentrating your only Kafka/Flink depth in one recent hire is fragile), while training gets someone building against the commitment immediately rather than waiting on a search outcome you don't control.\n\nMain tradeoff: pulling 2 of 7 engineers into an 8-week program on a team already thinned by attrition risks starving other work. I'd train just one mid-level engineer (~$12k) as the immediate hedge, and let the senior hire — once landed — absorb the second training slot's worth of capability through mentorship instead of a formal program. That keeps the total spend closer to $207k than $231k and limits the capacity hit to one person, not two.","ttft_ms":24591,"type":"result","duration_ms":29582,"uuid":"5e88a88c-9202-4118-804e-e87f301538ba","ttft_stream_ms":2476,"time_to_request_ms":80,"first_content_frame_ms":2476,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
